body:
### Description

After upgrading from `ai@5.0.0-beta.28` to `ai@5.0.0-beta.29`, TypeScript can no longer infer the correct types for tool inputs when filtering tool calls by name. This regression was introduced by PR #7595 which added support for dynamic tools.

Previously, filtering tool calls by name would correctly narrow the type of input. Now, even after checking the dynamic flag as suggested in the documentation, input remains typed as unknown, requiring explicit type assertions.

### Example

```typescript
import { generateText, tool } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

const result = await generateText({
  model: openai('gpt-4'),
  tools: {
    weather: tool({
      description: 'Get weather information',
      inputSchema: z.object({
        location: z.string(),
        unit: z.enum(['celsius', 'fahrenheit'])
      }),
    }),
  },
  prompt: 'What is the weather in NYC?',
});

// Before v5.0.0-beta.29: This worked without type assertions
const weatherCall = result.toolCalls.find(call => call.toolName === 'weather');
if (weatherCall) {
  console.log(weatherCall.input.location); // ✅ Typed as string
}

// After v5.0.0-beta.29: Even with dynamic check, type inference fails
const weatherCall2 = result.toolCalls.find(call => {
  if ('dynamic' in call && call.dynamic) {
    return false;
  }
  return call.toolName === 'weather';
});
if (weatherCall2) {
  console.log(weatherCall2.input.location); // ❌ Error: 'input' is of type 'unknown'

  // Requires explicit type assertion
  const input = weatherCall2.input as z.infer<typeof weatherInputSchema>;
  console.log(input.location); // ✅ Works with assertion
}
```

### Expected behavior


When filtering tool calls by name and checking the dynamic flag, TypeScript should be able to infer the correct type for input based on the tool definition, as shown in the documentation example.

### Impact

This breaks existing code that relied on TypeScript's type inference for tool calls, requiring developers to add explicit type assertions throughout their codebase when upgrading to the latest beta.

### AI SDK Version

- ai: 5.0.0-beta.29
- @ai-sdk/openai: 2.0.0-beta.13
